---
import { TOKENS, GLOSS, DEFAULT_TOKEN, ARC, MAT, attend, arcPath, matSize } from '../lib/attention';

const A = attend({ causal: false, scaled: true });
const sel = DEFAULT_TOKEN;
const { w: MW, h: MH } = matSize();
const top = (i: number) => {
  const row = A[i];
  const j = row.indexOf(Math.max(...row));
  return { j, v: row[j] };
};
const t0 = top(sel);
---

<figure class="att" data-attention>
  <ol class="att-steps">
    <li>Each token turns its vector into a <strong>query</strong> (what it is looking for) and a <strong>key</strong> (what it offers).</li>
    <li>The query is compared with every key by a dot product, divided by √d, and passed through a softmax. The result is one row of weights that sums to 1.</li>
    <li>The token's new vector is the weighted mix of every token's <strong>value</strong>.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="att-sentence">
    <svg class="arcs" viewBox={`0 0 ${ARC.w} ${ARC.h}`} preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
      {TOKENS.map((_, j) => (
        <path
          d={arcPath(sel, j)}
          data-arc={j}
          stroke-width={1 + 10 * A[sel][j]}
          stroke-opacity={0.25 + 0.75 * A[sel][j]}
        />
      ))}
    </svg>
    <div class="tokens" role="group" aria-label="Choose the token whose attention is shown">
      {TOKENS.map((t, i) => (
        <button type="button" data-token={i} aria-pressed={i === sel ? 'true' : 'false'} tabindex={i === sel ? 0 : -1}>
          {t}
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="att-readout" aria-live="polite" data-readout>
    “{TOKENS[sel]}” attends most to “{TOKENS[t0.j]}” ({t0.v.toFixed(2)}).
  </p>
  <p class="note att-gloss">{GLOSS} “berbattı” is split into the pieces “berbat” and “##tı”, the way WordPiece splits Turkish suffixes.</p>

  <div class="att-lower">
    <svg class="matrix" viewBox={`0 0 ${MW} ${MH}`} role="img" aria-labelledby="att-matrix-title">
      <title id="att-matrix-title">Attention matrix. Each row is a query token, each column a key token; darker cells mean more attention.</title>
      {TOKENS.map((t, j) => (
        <text x={MAT.left + (j + 0.5) * MAT.cell} y={MAT.top - 10} text-anchor="middle" class="m-label">{t}</text>
      ))}
      {TOKENS.map((t, i) => (
        <text x={MAT.left - 8} y={MAT.top + (i + 0.5) * MAT.cell + 5} text-anchor="end" class="m-label">{t}</text>
      ))}
      {A.map((row, i) =>
        row.map((v, j) => (
          <g>
            <rect
              x={MAT.left + j * MAT.cell + 1}
              y={MAT.top + i * MAT.cell + 1}
              width={MAT.cell - 2}
              height={MAT.cell - 2}
              class="m-cell"
              fill-opacity={Math.max(0.05, v)}
              data-cell={`${i}-${j}`}
            />
            <text
              x={MAT.left + (j + 0.5) * MAT.cell}
              y={MAT.top + (i + 0.5) * MAT.cell + 5}
              text-anchor="middle"
              class={v > 0.45 ? 'm-val m-val-on' : 'm-val'}
              data-cell-t={`${i}-${j}`}
            >
              {v.toFixed(2)}
            </text>
          </g>
        )),
      )}
      <rect
        x={MAT.left - 1}
        y={MAT.top + sel * MAT.cell - 1}
        width={MAT.cell * TOKENS.length + 2}
        height={MAT.cell + 2}
        class="m-row"
        data-rowmark
      />
    </svg>

    <div class="att-controls" data-controls hidden>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Model</legend>
        <label><input type="radio" name="att-mode" value="bert" checked data-mode /> BERT: every token sees every token</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="att-mode" value="gpt" data-mode /> GPT: a causal mask hides later tokens</label>
      </fieldset>
      <label class="att-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-scaled /> Divide scores by √d</label>
      <p class="note" data-explain>With the scaling, weights stay spread out. Turn it off to see the softmax collapse onto one token.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="note">
    Hand-set toy scores chosen to show patterns trained models tend to learn, such as an adjective attending to its noun and a suffix to its root. Not weights from a trained model. The softmax, the √d scaling and the mask are computed live in your browser.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { initAttention } from '../scripts/attention';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-attention]').forEach(initAttention);
</script>

<style>
  .att {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-5);
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .att-steps {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    padding-left: 1.4em;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .att-steps li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4em;
  }

  .att-sentence {
    position: relative;
  }

  .arcs {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 96px;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .arcs path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--leaf);
    vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }

  .tokens {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .tokens button {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .tokens button[aria-pressed='true'] {
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .tokens button:hover {
    border-color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .tokens button {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
  }

  .att-readout {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .att-gloss {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  .att-lower {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .att-lower {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .matrix {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .matrix text {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .m-label {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .m-cell {
    fill: var(--leaf);
  }

  .m-cell.m-masked {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--rule);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }

  .m-val {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .m-val-on {
    fill: var(--board);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .m-row {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }

  .att-controls[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .att-controls {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .att-controls fieldset {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    border: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .att-controls legend {
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .att-controls label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-height: 40px;
  }

  .att-controls input {
    accent-color: var(--leaf);
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    flex: none;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    max-width: 70ch;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
